			],
			"Message": "feat(Land): Enable native file watcher and add VS Code API coverage matrix\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to pull in Mountain-native search provider integration and PostHog exception cap. This commit also introduces comprehensive VS Code API documentation and enables Layer4 file watching.\n\nChanges:\n- **Search Provider (Element):** New land-native ISearchService implementation in Sky and Output that routes Search viewlet queries to Mountain's `search:findFiles` / `search:findInFiles` handlers. Resolves silent zero-result returns when filesystem is Mountain-based.\n- **PostHog Cap:** Add `LAND_POSTHOG_SKY_EXCEPTION_GLOBAL_LIMIT` (default 7) to respect CDN's ~10/10s ceiling and prevent rate-limit warnings during boot flurries.\n- **File Watcher:** Change `TierFileWatcher` from `Stub` to `Layer4`, enabling Mountain's native notify-crate backend (FSEvents/inotify/ReadDirectoryChangesW). This unblocks LSP-driven extensions from receiving disk mutation events.\n- **Documentation:** Add VSCode-API-Coverage-Matrix.md - a 419-line authoritative map of every `vscode.*` namespace, implementation track (Stock-Node/Rust-native), status, and planned migrations.\n\nImpact: Search now works with Mountain filesystem. Extension file watchers (ESLint, TypeScript, Tailwind) can now receive filesystem change events. Comprehensive API tracking document enables systematic dual-track implementation.",
			"SHA": "fc2622c3a692b211f0334ca5348ec5d09accd546"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T15:08:18Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5213,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Mountain): Add trusted system paths bypass and idempotent VSIX installs\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to pull in two extension-management improvements:\n\n1. **PathSecurity**: Add `IsTrustedSystemPath` that defines directories Land owns (`.land/`, Application Support, bundled extension roots, TMPDIR) which bypass the workspace-folder sandbox check. Enables the extension scanner to read `~/.land/extensions` for user-installed VSIXes.\n\n2. **VsixInstaller**: Remove `AlreadyInstalled` error and treat re-installs as no-op when target already exists with a readable manifest. Matches VS Code semantics and prevents renderer crash from null result dereference. Corrupt/partial installs are wiped and re-extracted.\n\nImpact: Unblocks the extension loading pipeline, allowing user-installed extensions to appear in the Extensions sidebar.",
			"SHA": "cd7b93cae75e5f404dd29196c38b4ed4d3b70f25"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-24T14:49:45Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				5213,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Update Element with status bar and command bridges\n\nSynchronize Element submodule to pull in cross-cutting integration changes:\n- **Output:** Enhance ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform to pre-resolve IStatusbarService, ICommandService, and CommandRegistry into globalThis.__CEL_SERVICES__ during workbench startup.\n- **Sky:** Wire status bar bridge for `vscode.window.createStatusBarItem()` routing through `IStatusbarService.addEntry()`. Add command bridge layers for `sky://command/{execute,register,unregister}` to invoke CommandsRegistry.\n- **Mountain:** Add payload preview (160 bytes) to notification-drop logging, register benign ENOENT paths for MCP config, snippets, keybindings, AI workspace, git config.\n- **Maintain:** Dependency bumps for pozil/auto-assign-issue and @cloudflare/workers-types.\n\nImpact: Extension-contributed status bar items now render in native VS Code DOM. Extension commands execute against the workbench with proper bidirectional binding.",
			"SHA": "dbf113f467dc000c8b394b7d00694e2025368ead"
		},
